meta {
  name: Refresh Unknown Token (401)
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "refreshToken": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
  }
}

docs {
  A token that was never issued. Expect 401 {"error": "Invalid refresh token"}.

  The important half is the NON-effect: this must revoke nothing. Check that
  your live session still works by running Refresh (seq 3) afterwards — it
  should still return 200.

  If posting garbage could revoke sessions, anyone could sign a user out by
  guessing, which turns the reuse-detection defence into a denial-of-service
  weapon.
}
